# Vitest / RTL

Tests live under `app/frontend/tests` mirroring `app/frontend`. Use Vitest + Testing Library. Playwright e2e stays under `app/frontend/tests/e2e` and talks to a real server.

## What to assert

Assert behavior that can break: roles, actions, hrefs that are contracts, callback/wiring payloads, one representative datum, and branches.

```tsx
expect(screen.getByRole("link", { name: /4 Active clients/i }))
  .toHaveAttribute("href", "/clients")
expect(screen.getByText("Lawrence Schultz")).toBeInTheDocument()
```

Prefer smoke checks for presentational chrome: children render, interactive region exists, accent CSS variable when that variable is the public contract (`tone="alert"`).

## Avoid

- Listing every `views.*` i18n key or chrome copy as text (`getByText("views.dashboard.clients.title")`)
- Pinning CSS-module / Linaria `className` strings unless the class is a behavioral API (e.g. calendar layout math, sidebar active state)
- Snapshot tests of large UI boards
- Asserting that prop strings passed into a header equal those same strings on screen

## Form and provider setup

- Forms: `remember={false}`; for form-context tests use Form from `use-inertia-form`, wrap with `MantineProvider`, stub `matchMedia` in `beforeEach`, wrap `Grid.Col` in `Grid`.
- Translated assertion stability (backend messages in shared flows): use a stable locale; frontend tests that mock `t` as identity should still assert roles/actions over key laundry lists.
